<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greben Cossacks</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greben <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> were a community of Cossacks who settled in the foothills and along the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek River</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> from the 16th century. Many were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-believers">Old Believers</a>, and they lived in close contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumyks">Kumyks</a>, adopting elements of their dress and customs. In the 18th century they were brought under Russian state control and later absorbed into the Terek Cossack Host.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greben-cossacks.jpg" alt="Greben Cossacks" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grigory Gagarin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sc%C3%A8nes,_paysages,_moeurs_et_costumes_du_Caucase_dessin%C3%A9s_d%27apr%C3%A9s_nature_par_le_prince_G._Gagarine.25.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
